  "notes": "The research is explicit that this is Bronx melodic trap and NOT drill, so nothing drill is authored — the snare stays on the trap parent's beat 3 and `relatedGenres` deliberately omits the drill models. What it is instead: functional 4-bar minor harmony (i–VI–III–VII and i–iv–VI–V, both researched) with 7ths on the piano voicings, and a drum layer explicitly described as supporting a song rather than driving it — which is authored as the lowest `fillDensity` and `openHat.prob` of the melodic entries here plus light rolls. The vocal's wide range and sustained hook tails give a raised `octaveJumpProb` over a moderate note count, and the harmonized double-track hooks are the counter's two-style pairing at `densityRatio` 0.52. ⚠ `medium`: the research rates construction medium-high but tempo range only medium, and the tempo band is the INFERRED parameter here — 130–150 with `mode` 140 is the era default, not a measurement of this catalog. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
